@@ -12,6 +12,8 @@ yamt's local conflict check (request `docs/slices/request-local-conflict-check.m
 
 Resolving a merge request's conflicts (plan §2 #139–#143) adds three `MergeRequestSource` methods, passed through unchanged by `tauriMergeRequests.ts` (`tauriResolve.test.ts`): `resolveMergeRequest(iid)` → `ResolveReply`, `continueMergeRequest(iid)` → `ContinueMergeReply`, `findLocalMerge()` → `LocalMerge`. Fixture mode (`?mr=<script>`) answers a resolve after a second as an open does: !640 `started` with conflicts, !632 `started` clean, !624 `refused` `localAhead`, !616 `windowFailed` "yamt: not found", any other `started`, on `feature/fixture-<iid>` into `main`; `findLocalMerge` is `free` until a `started` or `windowFailed`, then `merging { iid, windowOpen: false }`; `continueMergeRequest` of that iid answers `opened` (after a second) and from then `windowOpen: true`, of any other iid `ended`. Fixture mode's operation also takes ?mergeRequest=created|moved|unchanged|detached|same (Continue answers ReadyToPush), ?clean (no file listed), ?push=rejected (the first push fails) and ?leftovers (Abort leaves two).
 
+A row's people (plan §2 #151–#156): the author, assignees, reviewers (with their `ReviewState`) and approvers (`approvedBy`, GitLab's order) are domain `Person`s whose `picture` is the one address the `<img>` loads: `toMergeRequestPage(raw, uploadedPicture)` and `toRerequestReply(raw, uploadedPicture)` turn an `uploaded` picture into `uploadedPicture(username)` (in the app `convertFileSrc(username, PICTURE_SCHEME)`, `tauriMergeRequests.ts`, `yamt-picture://localhost/<username>`, 404 when none), a `gravatar` one into Rust's checked address as sent, `none` into `null` (initials); no other address is built. Labels keep their colours (`null` when GitLab's are not hex) and rows `mayRerequest`. `rerequestReview(iid, username)` → `RerequestReply` (`requested` carries the row's reviewers now). Fixture mode: every row has an author (the next of `PEOPLE`), review states cycling requested, reviewed, approved, changes requested, `approvedBy` the first `index % 4` people, `mayRerequest` false on every 9th row from index 8; every 8th row from index 2 (!638, …) has three reviewers besides its assignee in three states (dmitri a done one on !638); label colours are CSS colour names (`docs` none); !635 has a zero size; pictures are `data:` addresses only (sam and anna load, ben's does not decode, chiara and dmitri none: `fixtureUploadedPicture` stands in for the scheme). Its `rerequestReview` answers after 1,000 ms and logs `mergeRequests.fixture_rerequest`: dmitri `refused`, a non-reviewer `notReviewer`, any other reviewer `requested` with that reviewer back at `requested`.
+
 `localMergeDomain.ts` holds the merge window's aliases (MergeView, ReturnTo, Leftover, AbortReply, PushReply) over bindings; domain.ts's Listing and ChunkSource import from it.
 
 `tauri.ts` `readClipboard(selection)` reads the clipboard through the shell, never through WebKit (plan §2 #99): GTK's text request, `null` for unreadable or no text; `main.ts` hands it to `ui/linuxPaste.ts` `takeLinuxPastes` on Linux. The fence (PM8, `scripts/clipboardFence.ts`) is on WebKit's clipboard reads: `clipboardData` and `navigator.clipboard.read`/`readText` outside `ui/linuxPaste.ts`. `keys.ts` holds both platform tests: `isMac` (CodeMirror's `Mod`) and `isLinux` (the one Linux rule, also behind `showsAntialiasing`).
